HardenedBSD contributions in 5BSD
=================================

5BSD has adopted changes from HardenedBSD, https://hardenedbsd.org/.  We
thank the HardenedBSD Project and Shawn Webb for this work.

No HardenedBSD source tree is imported here.  The adopted changes were
ported into the native 5BSD files listed below.  This directory records
that credit and carries the HardenedBSD license (LICENSE, copied verbatim
from the HardenedBSD section of the HardenedBSD COPYRIGHT file at the
pinned revision).  The files they changed keep their existing copyright
and license notices.

Upstream
--------
Repository: https://rad.hardenedbsd.org/z2HLHXgL1xevBNQsf8BmQW7MpJmtm.git
Pinned revision: 377c16e8de65d1b5885c4aa26e404f37b90aa2ca
  (hardened/current/master at the 2026-09-24 audit; FreeBSD baseline
  fc544d3b57f27f1422969fca0002cb2bff30ab17)
License: LICENSE (BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2013-2026 The HardenedBSD
  Project)

Adopted changes
---------------
5BSD commit d74fc2b15d9 (2026-09-24), defensive fixes, adapted:
  usr.bin/logger/logger.c
    gethostname() failure and unterminated-buffer handling.
    HardenedBSD 2c4078dd70af and the retained hostname hardening.
  sys/dev/qlnx/qlnxe/qlnx_os.c
    qlnx_zalloc(): return NULL instead of passing a failed allocation to
    bzero().  HardenedBSD 4aefbf23f7bb.
  sys/dev/mrsas/mrsas.c, sys/modules/mrsas/Makefile
    mrsas_get_pd_list()/mrsas_get_ld_list(): release the reserved command
    and return ENOMEM when the temporary DCMD allocation fails.
    HardenedBSD ca99b1d7e369, 21e1924852dc; adapted (5BSD omits the
    mrsas_free_tmp_dcmd(NULL) calls and zeroes locally, because 5BSD does
    not enable HardenedBSD's blanket kernel allocation zeroing).
  tools/test/hardenedbsd/
    Fault-injection tests for the three fixes (5BSD-written).

5BSD commit 1d2e8d6e3f2 (2026-09-24), build default:
  share/mk/bsd.opts.mk, tools/build/options/WITHOUT_BIND_NOW,
  share/man/man5/src.conf.5
    BIND_NOW (full RELRO) enabled by default.  The mechanism already
    existed in FreeBSD; the default follows HardenedBSD acfca02404c1 and
    444d19dca3bd (Shawn Webb).

5BSD commit dd099d50037 (2026-09-24), jail(8):
  usr.sbin/jail/{config.c,jail.c,jailp.h,jailparse.y,state.c}
    emalloc() uses calloc() and erealloc() uses recallocarray().
    HardenedBSD ff27ee722b55c68f607b0d6b1113e9f9b9dfb9a4, "jail(8): Use
    safer memory management APIs" (Shawn Webb).
  usr.sbin/jail/tests/
    Regression tests (5BSD-written).

Adding to this record
---------------------
When another HardenedBSD change is adopted, add it above with the 5BSD
commit, the files changed, the HardenedBSD commit IDs and whether it was
copied, adapted, or reimplemented, and cite HardenedBSD in the commit
message.  If HardenedBSD source files are ever imported verbatim, place
them under this directory with their own notices.
